  "findings": "The adopted Dutch regulations and Study Guide establish 180 EC for the Dutch Media path. The first two years each have ten required 6 EC courses. Year three has 30 EC of open study, three 6 EC courses and a 12 EC individual thesis and colloquium. Entry to year two requires passing Academic English or Research Techniques. Entry to the second semester of year three requires passing year one and the year-two specialisation courses; thesis entry requires passing all courses in the first two years. The Dutch language test or refresher conditions the academic skills grade. Academic orientation and language testing carry no extra credits. The Media and Art routes have different research seminars and study trips. The regulations set the open-study approval and level requirements and allow a 12 EC internship with 18 EC of courses.",
  "authority": "Adopted Dutch OER dated 26 May 2026, art. 9.1 and annex 1 Dutch Art and Media plans on pp. 26–27. Its Dutch progression, attendance, open-study and language provisions control the Dutch comparator. The current study guide and exact seminar records distinguish Media AI and infrastructure research from Art exhibition catalogue and digital object registration. Article 10.2 gives the four equal specialisation choices in their official order. The Media illustration is chosen on that basis independently of UCR fit."
}
